The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**`. That path does
NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group — placing files there would not compile.
The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/`, where the
landed sibling P7 battery pages ship (EnergyPage, EnergyFlowPage, BatteryCellsPage,
BatteryDegradationPage, SleepEfficiencyPage — ledger status=done), and which `Sources` already lists as
a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups: true). Page hosting uses the proven
`*RouteRegistration` pattern chained in `Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift`. Tests live in
`apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Battery/`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only deviation
from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9 — identical to the reconciliation
used by every landed p4-apple P7 page.

The web route `/power-flow` had NO `AppRoute` case; this prompt adds `.powerFlow` (pathSegment
`power-flow`, group `.energy`, systemImage `bolt.horizontal.fill`) to `Sources/App/AppRoute.swift` so
`AppRouteParser` resolves `/power-flow` + the deep link automatically (its `parse(path:)` matches on
`pathSegment`), and wires the host in `TeslaSyncApp.swift`. ("navigation registration" is an allowed
file class.)

NAME-COLLISION GUARD (covenant #1): the module already compiles ~40 sibling `PowerFlow*` types from
`TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/*` (LivePowerFlowWidget / PowerFlowHistoryWidget — PowerFlowModel,
PowerFlowNode, PowerFlowArrow, PowerFlowSite, PowerFlowLiveStatus, PowerFlowStatRow, …). Every new
